prt-get 5.19.9 by Johannes Winkelmann, jw@tks6.net
Usage: prt-get <command> [options]
where commands are:

INFORMATION
  help                       show this help
  version                    show the current version
  list     [<filter>]        show a list of available ports
  printf   <format>          print formatted list of available ports
  listinst [<filter>][--depsort]  show a list of installed ports
  listorphans                list of ports with no packages depending on them
  info     <port>            show info about a port
  path     <port>            show path of a port
  readme   <port>            show a port's readme file (if it exists)
  dup                        Find duplicate ports
  isinst   <port1 port2...>  print whether ports are installed
  current  <port>            print installed version of port

DIFFERENCES / CHECK FOR UPDATES
  diff     <port1 port2...>  list outdated packages (or check args for change)
  quickdiff                  same as diff but simple format
          where opt can be:
    --all            display locked ports too
    --prefer-higher  prefer higher installed versions over lower ports
    --strict-diff    override prefer higher configuration setting

DEPENDENCIES
  depends   <port1 port2...>  show dependencies for these ports
  quickdep  <port1 port2...>  same as 'depends' but simple format
  deptree   <port>            show dependencies tree for <port>
  dependent [opt] <port>      show installed packages which depend on 'port'
          where opt can be:
                --all    list all dependent packages, not only installed
                --recursive    print recursive listing
                --tree         print recursive tree listing

SEARCHING
  search  <expr>     show port names containing 'expr'
  dsearch <expr>     show ports containing 'expr' in the name or description
  fsearch <pattern>  show file names in footprints matching 'pattern'

INSTALL, UPDATE and REMOVAL
  install [opt] <port1 port2...>    install ports
  update  [opt] <port1 port2...>    update ports
  grpinst [opt] <port1 port2...>    install ports, stop on error
  depinst [opt] <port1 port2...>    install ports and their dependencies
  remove [opt] <port1 port2...>     remove ports
          where opt can be:
                -f, -fi             force installation
                -fr                 force rebuild
                -uf                 update footprint
                -if                 ignore footprint
                -um                 update md5sum
                -im                 ignore md5sum
                -us                 update signature
                -is                 ignore signature
                --margs=<string>    pass 'string' to pkgmk
                --aargs=<string>    pass 'string' to pkgadd
                --rargs=<string>    pass 'string' to pkgrm
                --test              test mode
                --log               write log file
                --ignore=<package1,package2,...>
                                    Don't install/update those packages
                --pre-install       execute pre-install script
                --post-install      execute post-install script
                --install-scripts   execute pre-install and post-install script

SYSTEM UPDATE 
  sysup [opt]                       update all outdated ports
          where opt can be:
                --nodeps            don't sort by dependencies
                --test              test mode
                --log               write log file
                --prefer-higher     prefer higher installed versions over lower ones in ports tree
                --strict-diff       override prefer higher configuration setting
  lock <port1 port2...>             lock current version of packages
  unlock <port1 port2...>           unlock packages
  listlocked                        list locked packages

FILE OPERATIONS 
  ls <port>                         print a listing of the port's directory
  cat <port> <file>                 print out 'port/file'
  edit <port> <file>                edit 'port/file'

GENERAL OPTIONS
                -v                 Show version in listing
                -vv                Show version and decription in listing

                --path             Print path to port if appropriate (search, list, depends)

                --cache             Use a cache file
                --config=<file>     Use alternative configuration file
                --install-root=..   Use alternative install root directory
                --no-std-config     Don't parse default configuration file
                --config-prepend=.. Prepend '..' to configuration
                --config-append=..  Append '..' to configuration
                --config-set=..     Set configuration data '..',
                                       overriding config file
